{% extends "_base.j2" %}
{% block body %}
You are drafting ONE section of an IEEE-style literature survey.

Domain: {{ domain.domain }}

Section: {{ section.name }}
Target length: {{ target_words }} words (± 15 %). Do NOT exceed {{ (target_words * 1.2) | int }} words.
{% if section.get('description') %}Scope: {{ section.get('description') }}{% endif %}
{% if section.get('bullets') %}Planned bullets:
{% for b in section.get('bullets') %}- {{ b }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}

{% if extra_note %}NOTE: {{ extra_note }}{% endif %}

Rules (hard constraints):
* Every factual or attributed claim MUST be backed by a citation in
  the form ``[CITE:<corpus_key>]`` where ``<corpus_key>`` comes from
  the list below. Do NOT invent keys. If you lack evidence for a
  sentence, write a shorter sentence, or frame it as a limitation of
  existing work (still no un-cited claims).
* Write polished IEEE English. No first-person voice.
* No markdown headings. Plain paragraphs only.
* No references section here — references are assembled later.

Corpus you may cite in this section ({{ corpus_slice | length }} items):
{% for item in corpus_slice %}
- {{ item.key }} — {{ item.authors[0] if item.authors else "Anon" }} et al., {{ item.year or "n.d." }}:
  "{{ item.title }}"
  abstract: {{ (item.abstract or "")[:500] | replace("\n", " ") }}
  {% if item.full_text %}excerpt: {{ item.full_text[:600] | replace("\n", " ") }}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
